## Proven Implementation vs. Target Production Design

Lab work validated the **shape** of the system (replica → node sync → FUSE → CSI → app). Some internals used simpler stand-ins; production still targets the full design:

| Subsystem | Lab-proven baseline (kind & EKS) | Target production design |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **In-cluster Git replica** | Dumb HTTP static server + ConfigMap seeding | Smart HTTP (`git-http-backend` / Nginx) + automated `post-receive` hook |
| **FUSE engine** | Loopback FUSE over materialized commit directories | `go-fuse` lazy `git cat-file` over the bare object DB (no full tree materialize) |
| **Garbage collection** | Static retention / manual prune | Automated keep-set (trunk + tags + TTL + FUSE open-inode refs) |

