## Node Subsystem: Three Upgrade Domains

Think of three building staff with different blast radii:

| DaemonSet | Job (plain) | Job (technical) | Privileges | Upgrade |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **`git-reconciler`** | Keeps the local Git cache up to date | Watches ConfigMap, `git fetch`, writes `/mnt/git-storage/backend` | Host FS R/W | **Roll freely** — FUSE stays up |
| **`git-csi`** | Attaches the library door into each apartment | CSI `NodeServer`: host-ns bind-mount into the pod | `hostPID` + mount ns | **Roll freely** — active reads continue |
| **`git-fuse`** | Runs the librarian (virtual filesystem) | Owns `/dev/fuse`; exports `/mnt/git-storage/fuse` | `privileged`, `hostPID` | **Controlled only** — restart ⇒ local `ENOTCONN` |

**Why three processes, not one:** if FUSE and CSI share a pod, every CSI roll restarts FUSE and disconnects every app on that node. Splitting them is the core upgrade-domain decision.

